{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/358947-who-s-your-creator","id":358947,"title":"Who's Your Creator?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-04T02:55:02-08:00","id":358947,"title":"Who's Your Creator?","content":"Promethean: the Created is similar to Vampire, Changeling, and Geist in that there's a certain level of customization and story a player can put into their Sire/Keeper/and Geist at character creation. In Promethean's case it's who is/was your Creator? Was your Promethean the obsession fueled dream of a mad scientist? An attention crazed artist? Was your Created born by shear accident? Or was your sad cadaver just a stepping stone in someone else's Pilgrimage?<br /> <br /> I was led to this line of thinking while making a Galatea in celebration of the Firestorm Anthology's release and fast approaching Promethean: the Created 2E completion and ran into a wall when trying to make her Creator. I've never had trouble with this bit of background before with the above game lines, I'm especially fond of making True Fae personally, and discovered that a Promethean's Creator is singularly unique from the other's in that more than any other being who create supernatural creatures a Demiurge and Promethean spawn more Created only in times of personal desperation. While I still am having trouble coming up with my Promethean's Creator this gave me the idea to ask around about some of the most iconic Demiurges and Prometheans from the community's vast gaming experience. Who's your favorite Creator, and how did their obsession contribute to your character's journey through the Saturnine Nights?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Fixing spelling errors. 01-04-2015, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T14:57:21-08:00","id":359577,"title":"","content":"Dr. Magnus Angstrom was a high-ranking civilian roboticist working for the US Army (perhaps even TaskForce VALKYRIE). The General hired him to build an android that could infiltrate terrorist strongholds as one of their own and assassinate high-value targets; in no uncertain terms, he wanted a Terminator. And the General didn't care who he had to break to get one.<br /> <br /> Angstrom, despite his brilliance, had little luck with the project. As he kept hitting more and more snags, the General became more controlling. First hours were extended. Then he was given a cot for his lab. Then he was only given a few hours to visit with his wife and newborn daughter. All the while, the demands on the project kept expanding. Magnus was desperate, and considering &quot;alternative solutions&quot; to the project when they unearthed The Angel.<br /> <br /> A bizarre crystal vaguely in the shape of a Christmas tree topper, its atomic structure was ideal for circuitry. What's more, running electricity through it seemed to violate the laws of thermodynamics, and produced <i>more</i> energy than was run through it. What's more, it seemed to glow when in Magnus' presence. With the Angel, there would be no more barriers to progress. Magnus begged the General to be alone with it for a few days.<br /> <br /> Magnus began to build his Terminator prototype, which he quickly dubbed T1M (Terminator 1 Magnus). In a furor of design, construction, and lack of sleep, a robot soldier with built all while the glow of the Angel kept him awake. And when the power fed into the crystal was amplified before delivery to the creation, Magnus knew he had done the impossible.<br /> <br /> Especially when T1M asked questions like a precocious child, and went AWOL on his first armed assassination mission. The General didn't like that. Not at all. And thus Magnus was locked away without court martial, to work on a new version of T1M that would be more obedient.<br /> <br /> But Magnus knew he would never be able to replicate his results again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T19:02:39-08:00","id":359813,"title":"","content":"I'm currently entertaining two similar demiurges, both for Galateids. The first is a man driven to obsession by grief over the death of his wife, who mistakenly assumed that the Divine Fire will return her back to life; when the new Promethean rose from the slab, he verbally tore her down and fled. She's got some pretty severe abandonment issues and hates herself for not being the person who deserved love.<br /> <br /> The other is created as an ideal mate, but things quickly fall apart when it becomes apparent that the Promethean is transgender and cannot abide a relationship where they aren't allowed to be who they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T20:32:46-08:00","id":359837,"title":"","content":"I've yet to actually play a game of Promethean, but I have both free time and a fairly fertile imagination... so I've worked up an idea for a Tammuz character and have a general idea for his creator.<br /> <br /> Our Tammuz was actually made in a prison, after an inmate was killed without warning. One of the guards (possibly following Aurum?), feeling himself nearing the end of his Pilgrimage, managed to get his hands on the body, preparing and burying it in the prison yard. He wanted his creation to live free of confinement and the slavery common to their Lineage, but had a fairly unusual approach to the idea: in order to strive for freedom, his creation needed to be born in a cage with walls, bars and locks he could see.<br /> <br /> The result is a Ferrum practitioner who is more &quot;clever escape artist&quot; than &quot;relentless brawler&quot; who slips past prison security after the build-up of Disquiet eventually sparks a riot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","user":"Knowbody","date":".  Aurum, not Argentum! D'oh...! 01-05-2015, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T04:09:58-08:00","id":362285,"title":"","content":"Yes! I've finally been able to break through the wall. Thanks again everyone who shared in this topic. If you got any other great ideas for Creators feel free to continue to add them to the post. Here's what I finally decided on.<br /> <br /> Felix O'Hara was a unique child growing up. He was shy, awkward, and never quite made eye contact with anybody. He had a special talent though, he was a natural born artist. Instead of playing with the other children he would just draw all manner of things, and this talent was quickly recognized by his parents. He was a prodigy, eccentric but brilliant in a way only a great artist could be. Then, something bad happened. One night when Felix was about 13 years old a burglar broke into his some and in a struggle with his father the burglar accidentally shot and killed Felix's mother. That event sent both Felix and his father down a dark spiral, one where his father's fate may be explored in a different game line <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, and resulted in Felix being left in the care of his grandparents. The following years saw the now teenage artist delve into darker and more esoteric topics as he began to incorporate strange symbols into his artwork that he would later tell his therapist, one who he met with regularly in the years after his mother's death, came to him in a dream.<br /> <br /> It was during the latter half of his senior year that he made his first attempt, it was unsuccessful.<br /> <br /> His grandparents were out of town when they got the call from the hospital that their house had caught on fire and their grandson and his friends had barely made it out alive. When they got to the hospital they found that the doctors had to amputate Felix's left arm because it had sustained so much damage that it had become infected. One of his friends lost a leg to similar causes, and both Felix and his friends all claim that the fire was started by a lightning strike. This was not far from the truth, for a terrible storm blew into town the night the O'Hara residence burned down. A few days later the local cemetery would notice that one of the bodies had gone missing, Felix's mother no less, and while this was an extraordinary coincidence the authorities saw no link between the fire and the grave robbery. As Felix lay in recovery he sure hoped that the fire had killed them all...<br /> <br /> After his recovery Felix's grandparents found that this ordeal had given their grandson a new lease on life. His artwork was still dark and occult driven but now had a sense of spirituality to them. He also began to study the sciences with much greater vigor than before and even majored in it over the arts, which he still minored in, when he attended college. When asked about this his favorite response was, &quot;Science and Art are not mutually exclusive, both are meant to capture and define concepts that normally lie beyond our mortal scope of understanding.&quot; All in all it seemed that Felix O'Hara was well on his way to overcoming his hardships and becoming an outstanding member of society like his parents wanted. But beneath his newly cemented demeanor burned an obsession to spit in the eyes of god in cold fury for being so fickle with it's creations. He was dedicated to not fail a second time.<br /> <br /> And he did not.<br /> <br /> Hazel was made not to be a lover, or a missing loved one, or be loved at all really. The Galatea Lineage held the aesthetic essence and purity of form that Felix O'Hara felt most comfortable working with, nothing more. Her creation was meant to prove Felix for the genius his mother always knew he was, and her purpose was to exist as an affront to the laws of nature that allowed a accidental gunshot to ruin a child's life. She was his beautiful, perfect, aesthetic middle finger to the universe itself...but like all true artists and Demiurges as he examined his creation more thoroughly he began to see that she wasn't the perfect affront to god that he wanted. So he left, simple as that.<br /> <br /> Hazel's been looking for him ever since, at first just to understand why he left her alone but now more out of habit more than anything else. She's feels that if she can just find him then something will click and she will just understand what to do with her Pilgrimage next, or at least that's what she tells herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T07:30:23-08:00","id":365404,"title":"","content":"Nice, Dusksage! I may well crib that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T23:55:01-08:00","id":369514,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I'm glad you liked it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}